⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of The Video-Game Grammar
node SPW · SPW · ⟦The Video-Game Grammar:SPW:45ba28⟧

WHO   — The Video-Game Grammar — life rendered as a 16-bit game
WHAT  — The synth that renders heartbreak and growth in arcade terms: KOs and combos, extra lives, coins on defeat, a pee bar, the 1-UP, ‘L7,’ the X — diegetic and unquestioned.
WHERE — SPW · Scott Pilgrim vs. the World  Framework inputs: Scott Pilgrim vs. the World (2010); O'Malley's graphic novels  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because the film's deepest joke is that no one notices the game-logic; it is simply how being young and in love already feels — scored, leveled, and lethal.
HOW   — By HUD overlays, fighting-game flourishes, JRPG reward fanfares, and a coin-shower for every ex destroyed.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  Nobody here remarks that life is a video game — because to them it always was, KO and coins and all.

